{"slug":"l-a-rush","title":"L.A. Rush","desc":"PC, Midway 2005 (port of the Xbox game)","notes":["Read from cars/cars.dir + cars.res and pcars.dir + pcars.res with larush_formats.py (the parsing part of the L.A. Rush Blender importer import_larush.py).","The 36 player cars (folder names are the game's codes); <code>_kits.fbx shows the stock car and its body-kit version from pcars (p<code>: other bumpers, skirts, spoilers, bonnets, rims and decals) side by side, both visible.","A car is the LOD0 set of its parts put together through the part tree of the file: body with interior, steering wheel, glass, lamps and decals (Body); doors with their mirrors, bonnet, boot, bumpers and kit parts, wipers, plates (Parts); 4 wheels with their callipers (Wheels; lorries more).","Left out: the lower LOD sets (u1..u3), the shadow proxies (s0 / s2) and the shadow material, and the crash shape (every vertex also has a crumpled position in the files; the Blender importer loads it as a shape key).  The game's axes are right-handed (X forward, Y up, Z right, 10 cm units).","Paint: c_one = one red, as a small picture so that every viewer shows the same red; c_two (second colour) = near black. _Traffic: 46 traffic and story vehicles (01..20, buses, lorries, vans, taxi, police, lowriders ...); _Other: the plane, the train, the ship, the jet ski and the speedboat of the game; _Rims: the front left wheel (with calliper) of every player car and of its kit version (p<code>), outer face towards +X."],"tags":["l-a-rush"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["bu","",1329888,"l-a-rush","car-bu.zip","thumbs/l-a-rush/cars/car-bu.webp"],["ch","",1459513,"l-a-rush","car-ch.zip","thumbs/l-a-rush/cars/car-ch.webp"],["ci","",1443557,"l-a-rush","car-ci.zip","thumbs/l-a-rush/cars/car-ci.webp"],["cm","",1357412,"l-a-rush","car-cm.zip","thumbs/l-a-rush/cars/car-cm.webp"],["cr","",1516861,"l-a-rush","car-cr.zip","thumbs/l-a-rush/cars/car-cr.webp"],["dr","",1444997,"l-a-rush","car-dr.zip","thumbs